    "narrative": "The focal point of today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is **Travis Bazzana**, who anchors the 2B slot with an efficiency score of 60.94. Facing Nick Martinez and his 4.63 xERA, **Bazzana** benefits from a favorable matchup against a back-end starter, with a strong 15% boost derived from his current hot-hand recency and an expected #2 spot in the order. While his projected output is solid, the lack of depth in today\u2019s slate\u2014compounded by a team off-day for core speed threats like **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and **James Wood**\u2014forces us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. Without the stolen base production typically provided by **Carroll** or **Caballero**, we are operating below our desired ceiling, making every at-bat from **Bazzana** critical for maintaining our AVG floor.\n\nThe bench decision-making process was largely moot today due to the absence of games for high-upside players like **Josh Naylor**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain locked into the primary rotation when active. Had there been a full slate, **Brice Turang** would have been the first off the bench to challenge for a spot given his elite sprint speed profile, which remains our primary lever for closing the gap in the SB category. As it stands, the remaining active bench\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Mickey Moniak**\u2014will remain on standby to preserve our game caps. We are monitoring the official lineup card for **Bazzana** closely; should he be shifted down from the #2 hole, his score will see a marginal downward adjustment, though he remains the safest play in today\u2019s limited environment.",
